        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Both sides equal $n^4+2n^3-n^2-2n+1$.\n\nExpand the product and compare with part b.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}(n-1)n(n+1)(n+2)+1&=(n^2-1)(n^2+2n)+1\\\\(n-1)n(n+1)(n+2)+1&=n^4+2n^3-n^2-2n+1\\\\(n-1)n(n+1)(n+2)+1&=(n^2+n-1)^2\\end{align*}$$\nThe final equality follows from part b. Since $n^2+n-1$ is an integer whenever $n$ is an integer, this is a perfect square.",
